    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Uox9ehLxcz9BqHHYsi9gcd)_\n\nOpening an Org file failed with `Invalid association in tag alist: <<<<<<<`.\n\n**Cause (likely):** `main` has no conflict markers anywhere (checked with `git grep`), so the leftover is only in the local copy on the Mac. `sp-org-tag-registry.el` is a data file that `sp-org-tag-add` edits and `load-file`s, and a `<<<<<<< HEAD` line inside its quoted list reads as the symbol `<<<<<<<`, which Org rejects. The recent `Merge branch 'main'` commit is the probable source. The `git-gutter:live-update` error is probably a side effect of the failed mode setup; not confirmed.\n\n**To fix your copy:** open `~/.config/emacs-modular/libraries/modules/funct/sp-org-tag-registry.el`, keep both sides' tags, delete the `<<<<<<<`, `=======` and `>>>>>>>` lines.\n\n**This PR:**\n- `sp-org-tag-registry.el` drops non-tag entries (such as marker symbols) and shows a warning, so Org still starts.\n- `tools/check-conflict-markers.sh` and the `conflict-markers` workflow fail on leftover `<<<<<<<` / `>>>>>>>` lines (checked on a file with markers).\n- CHANGELOG entry.\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8u6NyvNdUHisSTGen)_",
